{# « Visible 1 sept. · rendu 15 oct. · dépassement bloqué · fichier » - the one line that says
   everything a document asks, composed here and nowhere else so the four screens that draw it
   cannot word it differently.

   Two of the four segments are addressed to whoever composed the dossier rather than to the cible:
   the day the document appeared is of no use to somebody already reading it, and whether the
   dépassement is allowed is the rule the screen itself applies - the dépôt closes or it does not.
   « Mes dossiers » therefore asks for the line without them.

   The two flags are read through `is defined` rather than `|default(true)`: that filter also fires
   on a *falsy* value, so `with_visibility: false` would have been handed straight back its default.

   Parameters: document, with_visibility (bool, default true), with_late (bool, default true). #}
{%- set show_visibility = with_visibility is defined ? with_visibility : true -%}
{%- set show_late = with_late is defined ? with_late : true -%}
{%- if show_visibility -%}
    {{- 'dossierRuleVisibleText'|trans({'%date%': document.visibleFrom|localized_date('d MMM')}) }} ·
{% endif -%}
{{ 'dossierRuleDueText'|trans({'%date%': document.dueOn|localized_date('d MMM')}) }} ·
{% if show_late -%}
    {{ (document.lateAllowed ? 'dossierRuleLateAllowedText' : 'dossierRuleLateBlockedText')|trans }} ·
{% endif -%}
{{ document.depositType.ruleKey|trans -}}
